FWIW the least worst solution to me seems to be removing the break together with the braces, so this `case` gets formatting like the `default` at the end:
https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/15ba42294eb57bd4850da0a830741c35aa8b46cc/src/script/interpreter.cpp#L1227-L1228

```diff
--- a/src/script/interpreter.cpp
+++ b/src/script/interpreter.cpp
@@ -675,18 +675,7 @@ bool EvalScript(std::vector<std::vector<unsigned char> >& stack, const CScript&
                 break;
 
                 case OP_RETURN:
-                {
                     return set_error(serror, SCRIPT_ERR_OP_RETURN);
-                }
-#if defined(__clang__)
-#pragma clang diagnostic push
-#pragma clang diagnostic ignored "-Wunreachable-code-break"
-#endif
-                break;
-#if defined(__clang__)
-#pragma clang diagnostic pop
-#endif
